-- Drops the reader's own picture along with the profile it belonged to.
--
-- The app no longer has a reader to name or draw: the library, its positions and
-- every setting are the device's rather than a person's. See `ReadingSummary`
-- for what is kept.
--
-- Dropped rather than left in place: it is the one table here holding a
-- photograph the reader chose from their own device, and keeping somebody's face
-- in a database nothing reads any more would be quiet hoarding.
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS profile_picture;
